# What the generator emits, pinned across changes to the generator.
#
# Two things already compare generated output and neither pins it: the
# determinism check diffs two runs of one binary, and the parity check
# diffs this implementation against the twin at the same revision. Both
# pass unchanged if a generator edit moves what every instance means,
# because both sides move together.
#
# This pins the other axis. For each admitted instance the corpus
# carries the vocabulary in the canonical form its digests are taken
# over, and the identity of the artifact that vocabulary seals. A
# refactor of the emitter is expected to leave both untouched; a change
# to what an instance means is expected to move them, and then the diff
# is where the author says so.
#
# The canonical form is what is pinned, not the emitted bytes, because
# the digests are taken over the canonical form: an entry's spelling —
# its whitespace, its key order — reaches nothing. That is what makes
# restructuring the emitter safe and a content change loud.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t

# RUN: zkc-family %S/Inputs/frik2.json --emit-vocabulary=%t/frik2.json --emit-spine=%t/frik2.mlir
# RUN: zkc-registry-lint %t/frik2.json | diff %S/Expected/frik2.vocabulary.json -
# RUN: zkc-opt '-pir-seal=protocol-vocabulary=%t/frik2.json construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json' %t/frik2.mlir | grep -oE 'id "[0-9a-f]{64}"' | head -1 | diff %S/Expected/frik2.identity -

