# The pin is not vacuous: the same instance with one parameter moved
# emits a different vocabulary and seals to a different identity, so a
# diff against these files means what it says.
# RUN: %python -c "import json,sys; d=json.load(open(sys.argv[1])); d['grinding_bits']=d['grinding_bits']+1; json.dump(d, open(sys.argv[2],'w'))" %S/../Oir/Inputs/plonky3-fri-vf.json %t/moved.json
# RUN: zkc-family %t/moved.json --emit-vocabulary=%t/moved.vocab.json --emit-spine=%t/moved.mlir
# RUN: zkc-opt '-pir-seal=protocol-vocabulary=%t/moved.vocab.json construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json' %t/moved.mlir | grep -oE 'id "[0-9a-f]{64}"' | head -1 | not diff %S/Expected/plonky3-fri-vf.identity -

# What the family mints, and what it may not redefine.
#
# Seal is fail-closed against a closed vocabulary, and for a generated
# instance that vocabulary comes from the same tool that wrote the spine
# it will judge. For entries the family mints for itself that is the
# arrangement working — the seal judgment holds the spine to a contract,
# whoever wrote it. For entries that also exist in the repository's
# registry it is not: a generator could redefine one and then satisfy
# its own redefinition, and seal would pass over a protocol that means
# something else. So every shared identifier carries the same definition
# on both sides, for every instance rather than for a chosen one, since
# the instances differ in which entries they share.
#
# Two entries differ by design and are exempt with their reasons: the
# FRI reduction contract is depth-parameterized, and a value-faithful
# instance's proof-of-work nonce is a one-word value where the base
# form's is a digest. An exemption for an entry an instance does not
# carry says nothing about it; one for an entry it carries and does not
# redefine fails, because a stale exemption hides the next drift.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/vocabulary-drift.py %zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json %t/frik2.json %t/friquarter.json %t/vf.json %t/real.json %t/bound.json | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DRIFT
# DRIFT: shared identifiers across 5 instances, {{[0-9]+}} exempt, none redefined
